================================================================================
DATA NOTICE
================================================================================

This software reads publicly accessible pages. It does not authenticate,
bypass access controls, or circumvent any security measure.

The MEP appointments registry contains personal data of identified individuals,
including full names and national identification numbers (cédulas). This
software processes that data locally, never transmits it to any third party.

Exported workbooks leave out the two columns that identify a person, the cédula
and the full name, unless whoever exports asks for them with the
--datos-personales option. CVM_EXPORT_PERSONAL_DATA sets the default for every
interface. A workbook written with those columns included is personal data and
has to be handled as such.

National identification numbers are removed from everything written to the log
files and to the terminal, including text quoted from the source pages and text
inside tracebacks. Names are not removed from log output, because no pattern can
tell one from an institution or a regional office name; nothing written today
puts one there.

Results shown on screen name the person appointed but never their cédula.

Users who redistribute data obtained with this tool are solely responsible for
compliance with Costa Rica's Ley 8968 (Ley de Protección de la Persona frente
al tratamiento de sus datos personales) and any other applicable law.

Test fixtures included in this repository are anonymized: all names and
identification numbers have been replaced with synthetic values.


